      meta: 'Published on May 6, 2026 · 6 min read',
      body: `<p class="intro-lead">Technical SEO is the base that allows a website to be crawlable, fast, understandable and usable. Without that base, even good content can perform worse than expected.</p><p>On a business website, technical SEO should not be seen as something reserved for large projects. Many improvements are simple, but they have a direct impact on indexation, user experience and trust.</p><h2>1. Indexation and important pages</h2><p>The first step is checking that Google can access the pages that matter: home, services, articles, legal pages and contact. It is also worth reviewing that duplicate pages, tests or low-value URLs are not indexed.</p><h2>2. Speed and page weight</h2><p>A slow website loses users and makes crawling harder. Images that are too heavy, unnecessary scripts or styles loaded without control can turn a simple page into a heavy experience.</p><ul><li>Compress images and use modern formats</li><li>Avoid libraries that do not add real value</li><li>Reduce blocks during initial loading</li><li>Review mobile performance, not only desktop</li></ul><h2>3. Clear HTML structure</h2><p>Headings, titles, links and sections help explain what each page is about. A single clear H1, well-ordered H2 headings and descriptive links are usually more useful than a beautiful but confusing visual structure.</p><h2>4. Metadata and URLs</h2><p>Each page should have a title, a description and a URL that explain its content. This does not guarantee rankings, but it helps improve understanding, clicks and consistency in search results.</p><h2>5. Internal linking</h2><p>Technical SEO also includes how pages connect. If an important service is isolated, it is harder for both the user and the search engine to find it. Articles can reinforce services, frequent questions and use cases.</p><div class="highlight-box"><p><strong>The technical side of SEO does not replace content.</strong> It gives content a solid base to be found, read and understood.</p></div><p>At <a href="https://jjodevelopers.com/" style="color:#60a5fa;">JJO</a> we review the technical side from development so the website does not carry problems that are difficult to correct later.</p><div class="cta-section"><p>If your website loads slowly or does not appear well on Google, we can review its technical base.</p><a href="https://jjodevelopers.com/" class="btn-cta">Visit JJO</a></div>`
